# Docs/spec/reference/cli.md: `jet check Core` reports no lint in Core source, nor one in a codec body
# the compiler generates for a Core type. The every-body check demands core.db's DBError codec, whose
# body grows a list in a loop of a core.mem module; its lint is Core's own, so a clean Core prints
# only the verdict. Unlocated, that lint printed here against the check's scratch entry.
env: NO_COLOR=1
step: jet check {root}/Core
exit: 0
stdout+stderr: ~ "has no problems" # the verdict line; the path varies with the checkout
stdout+stderr: !~ "Warning" # no lint without a real source path
